# Line endings. The repository stores LF, and every text file is checked out in LF whatever core.autocrlf says: Git
# for Windows sets it to true for the whole machine, which put a "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every add
# and left the working tree half LF, half CRLF. Lua (Windower), JavaScript, Python and the docs all read LF.
# Shell scripts above all: bash cannot run a script with CR at the end of its lines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Windows scripts: stored in LF like the rest, checked out in CRLF (cmd.exe needs it for its labels)
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
